<resources>

    <!--
      API 31+ (Android 12 and later) ONLY.

      From API 31 the SYSTEM owns the splash screen: `android:windowBackground` no longer
      controls it, so the values/ theme alone would leave Android 12+ devices on the platform
      default while API 24–30 got the canvas. Two files, one per range, is the whole reason
      this directory exists.

      No androidx.core:core-splashscreen dependency: setting the platform attribute directly
      does the same job for a static colour and adds nothing to the build.

      ACCEPTED DIVERGENCE (owner ruling 2026-08-02): the system also centres
      the launcher icon here, while iOS shows plain canvas. Forcing parity needs a transparent
      windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon, which fights the platform and breaks on OS updates.

      @color/splash_canvas is GENERATED — never hardcode a hex.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:editTextBackground">@drawable/rn_edit_text_material</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/splash_canvas</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_canvas</item>
    </style>

</resources>
